# L §5.11: "Windows compare by §4.4: ... argmin and argmax give the key whose value is decided below (above) every
# other key's, and otherwise HOLE-IMPRECISE."  d[a] is window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-10), d[b] = 2026-04-01,
# d[c] = window(2026-03-05, 2026-04-15).  argmin over a, b: a's whole window lies below 2026-04-01, so a.
# argmin over a, c: the windows overlap, neither is decided below the other: HOLE-IMPRECISE.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

index ks = [a, b, c]
input d[k in ks]: date
def m1: key ks = argmin(d[k] for k in ks where k != c) at reader
def m2: key ks = argmin(d[k] for k in ks where k != b) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  d[a] = window(2026-03-01, 2026-03-10)
  d[b] = 2026-04-01
  d[c] = window(2026-03-05, 2026-04-15)

ask q1: m1 law 2026-06-30
ask q2: m2 law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: a
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q2: ?"date within ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
